    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute is decided on the trip's own evidence, and the outcome is that the $4.50 no-show cancellation fee stands as charged and the driver is paid the platform's 80% share, $3.60.\n\nWhy the fee stands. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four parts of POL-NS-01 hold. They do. (a) The trip record (EV-TRIP-02752, weight 1.0) carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 22:06:11. (b) The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02752, weight 1.0) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at and after that moment: 44 accuracy-qualifying fixes in one unbroken in-geofence run opening at 22:06:11, with a closest approach of 0.0 m and POL-NS-02's three-consecutive-fix test met. The STANDARD zone class is read from the trip record, not assumed. (c) That single run lasts 434 seconds (22:06:11 to 22:13:25), comfortably above the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is null, so no longer threshold applies) — a surplus of 254 seconds. The dwell is measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not the tap, and the two are the same second (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0). (d) There is no boarding (started_at and ended_at are null) and the driver terminated at 22:13:25 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, well after the required dwell elapsed at 22:09:11.\n\nPOL-NS-05 is not engaged: the arrival tap coincides with the first in-geofence fix, so the trace does not put the driver more than 300 m from the pin or moving at 15 km/h at the marker; there is no false arrival and no false-arrival referral.\n\nThe rider's routes were each tested and each fails. POL-NS-06 has no shortfall to refund — the dwell exceeds the minimum by 254 seconds (the cited advisory limb is irrelevant, and in any case no advisory covers this pickup). POL-NS-02 / POL-NS-12: the arrival marker is a driver BUTTON press, not GPS_AUTO, so the platform's timing events do not substitute for the export — but the export itself carries the arrival and the dwell, so the limb is met on the trace. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02752) holds a single message and it is the driver's ('im at the pickup point', 22:06:31), so limb (a) fails; and the rider's own track places the rider's device 866–874 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m radius, so limb (c) affirmatively fails. Rider position is not an element of POL-NS-01, so this neither establishes nor defeats the charge. The filed words 'cancelled on me again' find no support in the record: rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both counterparty-dispute counters are 0.\n\nDriver compensation. POL-NS-07 sets the payout at 80% of the $4.50 net cancellation fee in force = $3.60; the rider's gross figure ($6.61) is not used. The anti-farming check does not trip and requires both limbs: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 3 (below 4) and 3 / 40 completed_trips_30d = 0.075 (below 0.08). The driver's lifetime prior_no_show_flags of 7 is not the field POL-NS-07 reads and has been given no weight whatever. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee, so the charge stands (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) and the case produces DRIVER_COMPENSATION; per POL-GEN-03 the amount_sgd field carries the same $3.60, being the money this ruling moves.\n\nIntegrity, escalation and execution. No POL-NS-08 impairment applies: there is no clock skew (arrival, dwell and termination timestamps agree across the trip record and the trace), no trace gap (100% coverage, 0 s maximum gap, 100 fixes, both tracks present), no chat defect (1 message matches trip_record.chat_message_count) and no fare defect (the $4.50 fare line equals the $4.50 in force). No POL-NS-09 trigger is present, so the case does not escalate. The only artifact below full weight is the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02752-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); it carries no fact for either party and does not affect this outcome. The monetary effect ($3.60) is below the $8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so the ruling executes automatically, and either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION","amount_sgd":3.6,"driver_compensation_sgd":3.6,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"To the rider and the driver: the $4.50 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-02752 stands, and the driver is paid $3.60 under POL-NS-07. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold. (a) The trip record EV-TRIP-02752 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 22:06:11. (b) The GPS export EV-GPS-02752 carries the arrival itself: 44 accuracy-qualifying fixes fall inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, the qualifying in-geofence run opens at 22:06:11 — the same second as the marker — and the driver's closest approach to the pin is 0.0 m (POL-NS-02). (c) The effective dwell, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the tap, is 434 seconds (22:06:11 to 22:13:25) against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this STANDARD trip (platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is null), a surplus of 254 seconds. (d) No boarding event is recorded and the driver terminated at 22:13:25 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell had elapsed. The fee therefore stands and POL-NS-07 fixes the payout at 80% of $4.50 = $3.60, the figure the fare breakdown's own money block computes. Because the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd as POL-GEN-03 requires; the rider's own charge is not refunded.

The rider's points are answered, and the ones that matter are accepted. The rider is right that POL-NS-12 does not apply — the arrival marker is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO — but nothing turns on it, because the arrival and the wait are established by the GPS export in its own right, not by the marker. The rider is right that POL-NS-04 does not exonerate (the only chat message is the driver's at 22:06:31; the rider sent nothing; no admissible rider fix lies inside the 100 m rider-presence radius — 70 fixes, minimum 866.6 m — so limbs (a) and (c) fail), and right that there is no POL-NS-05 false marker (offset 0.0 s, no motion at the marker) and no POL-NS-06 shortfall. Those concessions remove routes against the fee; none of them establishes a route for it, and the driver's four limbs are carried on his own evidence.

On integrity: no artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08. The trace has 100% coverage with no gap and matches the arrival timestamp; the chat is complete against trip_record.chat_message_count; and the $4.50 fare line reconciles to platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so POL-NS-08(d) raises no defect. EV-ADVIS-02752-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT): it carries no fact for either side and only makes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation limb unavailable, which the driver does not need on a single continuous 434-second run. It is the only sub-1.0 artifact in the bundle and it decides nothing, so the finding rests on artifacts at weight 1.0 and no discount applies. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 3, below the 4-or-more limb; 3 / 40 = 0.075, below the 0.08 rate limb), no two admissible artifacts contradict each other, and there is no counterparty-dispute pattern. The driver's lifetime prior_no_show_flags = 7 is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used. The monetary effect is $3.60, below the $8.00 POL-GEN-05 threshold, so it executes automatically on issue, subject to the POL-GEN-04 appeal route."},"discarded_claims":[]}
